## Planning dispatch at initial implementation MR

Under [lifecycle policy](../../.agents/skills/restruct-sdlc/sdlc-management/references/roles-lifecycle.md#automatic-planning-after-integration),
an eligible next task with an existing ready Goal/Spec receives an automatic
provisional planning-only dispatch when the predecessor implementation MR first
opens, including a draft. Verify MR/source/target/candidate; do not wait for CI/Duo
or merge. Planning-only/placeholder/probe MRs do not qualify. Include baseline, current owner and provisional gates;
receipt is not implementation approval. Preserve specific owner holds.

## Execution dispatch after reviewed integration

Cite the [supervisor's reassessment/release](../../.agents/skills/restruct-sdlc/sdlc-management/references/roles-lifecycle.md#automatic-reassessment-and-execution-release),
reviewed predecessor integration, pending qualification, verified closed start gates
and task owner. Isolated implementation may overlap staging CI; final predecessor
ACCEPT still gates successor integration/final acceptance. No extra owner prompt
after recorded release; Plan/merge/CI alone grants none. Verify receipt and
acknowledgment; specific owner holds and native permissions remain.

## Coordinator milestone priority

Follow the [final-status convention](../../.agents/skills/restruct-sdlc/sdlc-management/references/coordination.md#coordinator-final-status-line).
A pending decision/review takes priority over another task's routine progress. Name the actionable task and use
`question`/`review-ready`, not `working`. The observer also notices explicit pending handoffs in a working
marker's summary without reopening historical body prose. Notices still grant no authority.
Summaries over the recommended 240 characters still classify within the existing transcript-row limit;
truncate only the delivered excerpt to 240 characters, after detecting pending handoffs in the full summary.

